==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|*forestrie}}, {{m|enm|*forsterie}} (suggested by {{m+|enm|forster}}, {{m|enm|forester|t=forester}}), from {{der|en|fro|foresterie}}, from {{m|fro|forest}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|fŏrʹ-ĭst-rē}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈfɒɹ.ɪst.ɹi/}}
** {{a|en|US}} {{IPAfont|/ˈfɔɹ.ɪst.ɹi/}}
** {{a|en|UK}} {{IPAfont|/ˈfɒɹ.ɪst.ɹi/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vininn126-forestry.wav|a=US}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈfɑɹ.ɪst.ɹi/|a=NYC}}
* {{hyphenation|en|for|est|ry}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒɹɪstɹi|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The science of planting and growing [[trees]] in [[forests]].
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The art and practice of planting and growing trees in forests.
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} The art and practice of [[cultivating]], [[exploiting]] and renewing forests for commercial purposes.
# {{lb|en|uncountable}} Commercial [[tree]] farming.
# {{lb|en|countable}} A tree farm.
# {{lb|en|countable}} A forest-covered area.

